The '''2023 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2023 FIFA Club World Cup]], an international club [[association football|football]] tournament hosted by [[Saudi Arabia]]. It was the 20th final of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised tournament between the club champions from each of the six continental confederations, as well as the host nation's league champions.

The match was played at the [[King Abdullah Sports City Stadium]] in [[Jeddah]] on 22 December 2023.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/439508d6da35a1dd/original/FIFA-Club-World-Cup-Saudi-Arabia-2023-Match-Schedule.pdf |title=Match Schedule: FIFA Club World Cup Saudi Arabia 2023 |publisher=[[FIFA]] |date=6 November 2023 |access-date=7 November 2023 |archive-date=10 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010145212/https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/439508d6da35a1dd/original/FIFA-Club-World-Cup-Saudi-Arabia-2023-Match-Schedule.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref> It was contested by English club [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]], representing [[UEFA]] as the reigning champions of the [[UEFA Champions League]], and Brazilian club [[Fluminense FC|Fluminense]], representing [[CONMEBOL]] as the reigning champions of the [[Copa Libertadores]].

Manchester City won the match 4–0 for their first FIFA Club World Cup title.

